{"step_index":407,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-24T23:54:16Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-24T18:54:16-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-24T18:54:17-05:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/<user>/Downloads/GTA6.Xbox.v1.0.2.1-CYBERLEEK/gta6_mission_flow_chart.md`\nTotal Lines: 286\nTotal Bytes: 13530\nShowing lines 1 to 150\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Grand Theft Auto VI: Campaign Mission Flow & Prerequisite Guide\n2: \n3: This document maps the mission dependency graph, prerequisite unlock trees, character-switching milestones, heist setup pipelines, and points of no return across the 5 story chapters of *Grand Theft Auto VI*.\n4: \n5: ---\n6: \n7: ## 1. High-Level Campaign Architecture\n8: \n9: The GTA VI storyline progresses through five distinct geographical and thematic narrative blocks. While open-world exploration is available between operations, missions operate in a strict Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) with key narrative bottlenecks connecting each chapter.\n10: \n11: ```mermaid\n12: flowchart TD\n13:     subgraph P[\"Prologue & Chapter 1\"]\n14:         C1[\"Just Like Paradise<br/>(Leonida Keys & Key Lento)\"]\n15:     end\n16: \n17:     subgraph C2B[\"Chapter 2\"]\n18:         C2[\"Paradise Lost<br/>(Port Gellhorn & Kelly County)\"]\n19:     end\n20: \n21:     subgraph C3B[\"Chapter 3\"]\n22:         C3[\"Tits, Ass, Drug Money<br/>(Vice City Outskirts & Metro Cartels)\"]\n23:     end\n24: \n25:     subgraph C4B[\"Chapter 4\"]\n26:         C4[\"Vice City, Baby<br/>(Vice City Metro & Ocean Beach)\"]\n27:     end\n28: \n29:     subgraph C5B[\"Chapter 5\"]\n30:         C5[\"Top of the World, Ma!<br/>(Climax & Resolution)\"]\n31:     end\n32: \n33:     C1 -->|\"Bottleneck: Discharge Time\"| C2\n34:     C2 -->|\"Bottleneck: Checking Out\"| C3\n35:     C3 -->|\"Bottleneck: Ocean Beach\"| C4\n36:     C4 -->|\"Point of No Return: Sunset\"| C5\n37: ```\n38: \n39: ---\n40: \n41: ## 2. Chapter 1: Just Like Paradise (Leonida Keys)\n42: \n43: ### Mechanics & Structure\n44: - **Playable Character**: Strictly locked to **Jason** (with Lucia introduced in the Prologue and reunited in *\"Coming Home\"*).\n45: - **Core Narrative**: Petty smuggling, local debt enforcement for Brian, and settling in Key Lento following Lucia's release from Hamlet State Penitentiary.\n46: - **Critical Milestone**: Completing *\"Island Dreams\"* opens local diving and strand activities; *\"Tourist Trap\"* begins the irreversible sequence into Chapter 2.\n47: \n48: ```mermaid\n49: flowchart TD\n50:     M01[\"1. Prologue<br/>(Lucia Prison Interview)\"] --> M02[\"2. Gone Fishing<br/>(Jason & Donnie Smuggling)\"]\n51:     M02 --> M03[\"3. Gear Up<br/>(Brian's Armory)\"]\n52:     M03 --> M04[\"4. Just a Scratch<br/>(Ganado Repair)\"]\n53:     M04 --> M05[\"5. Lab Fees<br/>(Brian's Rent Collection)\"]\n54:     \n55:     M05 --> M06[\"6. Unwanted Attention<br/>(Cal's Hamlet Trip)\"]\n56:     M06 --> M07[\"7. Pipework<br/>(Marina Odd Jobs)\"]\n57:     M07 --> M08[\"8. Hey Arnold!<br/>(Broker Interrogation)\"]\n58:     M08 --> M09[\"9. Island Dreams<br/>(Keys Diving Unlocked)\"]\n59:     M09 --> M10[\"10. Feng Shui<br/>(Moving Furniture)\"]\n60:     \n61:     M10 --> M11[\"11. Coming Home<br/>(Lucia Released from Prison)\"]\n62:     \n63:     M11 --> M12[\"12. Clean Up After Donnie\"]\n64:     M12 --> M13[\"13. Buck Me<br/>(Banking App Setup)\"]\n65:     M13 --> M14[\"14. Down to Earth<br/>(Marina Drug Run)\"]\n66:     M14 --> M15[\"15. Clear Skies<br/>(Southwind Bikers)\"]\n67:     \n68:     M15 --> M16[\"16. Day Release<br/>(Rusty Anchor Night Out)\"]\n69:     M16 --> M17[\"17. Swamped<br/>(Kingfishers Smugglers)\"]\n70:     M17 --> M18[\"18. Don Gone<br/>(Clearing Donnie's Trailer)\"]\n71:     M18 --> M19[\"19. Recalibration<br/>(Cal Intervention)\"]\n72:     \n73:     M19 --> M20[\"20. Tourist Trap<br/>(Mattia's Offer - Transition Starts)\"]\n74:     M20 --> M21[\"21. Home Sweet Home<br/>(Key Lento Fallout)\"]\n75:     M21 --> M22[\"22. Discharge Time<br/>(Chapter 1 Climax)\"]\n76: ```\n77: \n78: ---\n79: \n80: ## 3. Chapter 2: Paradise Lost (Port Gellhorn)\n81: \n82: ### Mechanics & Structure\n83: - **Playable Character**: Heavily centered on **Lucia** during early recovery, then **permanently unlocks Dual Character Switching** via *\"Coffee Break\"*.\n84: - **Vehicle Fencing**: Unlocked via *\"Moses\"* (enabling Slim Jim vehicle thefts and custom garage registrations).\n85: - **Narrative Bottleneck**: *\"Checking Out\"* concludes Port Gellhorn motel residency and moves operations to Vice City.\n86: \n87: ```mermaid\n88: flowchart TD\n89:     C1_End[\"From Ch. 1: Discharge Time\"] --> M23[\"23. What's in the Bag?<br/>(Starlet Motel Arrival)\"]\n90:     M23 --> M24[\"24. Overnight Charges\"]\n91:     M24 --> M25[\"25. Take Care of Jason<br/>(Lucia Solo Medical Run)\"]\n92:     M25 --> M26[\"26. Just Moved In\"]\n93:     \n94:     M26 --> M27[\"27. Girls' Trip\"]\n95:     M27 --> M28[\"28. Moses<br/>(Vehicle Fencing Unlocked)\"]\n96:     M28 --> M29[\"29. New Look\"]\n97:     M29 --> M30[\"30. How Do I Look?\"]\n98:     M30 --> M31[\"31. Behind on Payments\"]\n99:     \n100:     M31 --> M32[\"32. Ambulance Chaser\"]\n101:     M32 --> M33[\"33. Painkiller Supplier\"]\n102:     M33 --> M34[\"34. Daily Driver\"]\n103:     M34 --> M35[\"35. Pick Up A Gun\"]\n104:     M35 --> M36[\"36. Slam Dunk\"]\n105:     M36 --> M37[\"37. Breakfast Run\"]\n106:     \n107:     M37 --> M38[\"38. Coffee Break<br/>★ UNLOCKS DUAL CHARACTER SWITCHING ★\"]\n108:     \n109:     M38 --> M39[\"39. Hit Avery Pawn<br/>(Robbery System Demo)\"]\n110:     M39 --> M40[\"40. Hit Kingpin Bowling\"]\n111:     M40 --> M41[\"41. Impounded Vehicle\"]\n112:     M41 --> M42[\"42. Afternoon Delight\"]\n113:     M42 --> M43[\"43. Prepare for Vice City\"]\n114:     M43 --> M44[\"44. Checking Out<br/>(Move to Vice City)\"]\n115: ```\n116: \n117: ---\n118: \n119: ## 4. Chapter 3: Tits, Ass, Drug Money (Vice City Infiltration)\n120: \n121: ### Mechanics & Structure\n122: - **Scope**: Largest chapter in the game (26 main missions).\n123: - **Key Factions & The 3 Parallel Alliance Strands**: Upon completing *South Leonida Real Estate* (establishing the Vice City safehouse), three major alliance storylines unlock concurrently:\n124:   1. **Tyrone Strand (Street Muscle)**: Missions 51 & 52.\n125:   2. **Boobie Ike & Dre'Quan Strand (Syndicate & Nightclub)**: Missions 54, 55, & 56.\n126:   3. **Raul Bautista & Randy Strand (Cartel Logistics & Exotic Cars)**: Missions 53, 57, 58, 59, & 60.\n127: - **Dynamic Interleaving vs. Concurrent Map Pins**: In casual play, waiting allows all three contacts to be active simultaneously as map pins. In speedrunning, finishing a mission places that contact on a brief cooldown timer while another contact rings, causing an optimal Any% runner to zigzag between Tyrone, Boobie, and Raul with zero downtime.\n128: - **Major Heist**: **The Sinfrontera National Bank Heist**. All 3 strands converge at *Mission 61: Sinfrontera National Bank Scope Out*, unlocking the modular heist preparation board and culminating in *Mission 70: The Cartel Heist* ($10.5M Take).\n129: \n130: ```mermaid\n131: flowchart TD\n132:     C2_End[\"From Ch. 2: Checking Out\"] --> M45[\"45. Welcome to Vice City\"]\n133:     M45 --> M46[\"46. Dealer's Choice\"]\n134:     M46 --> M47[\"47. Meet the Heders\"]\n135:     M47 --> M48[\"48. Dubious Provenance\"]\n136:     M48 --> M49[\"49. Mami Knows Best\"]\n137:     M49 --> M50[\"50. South Leonida Real Estate<br/>(Vice City Safehouse Unlocked)\"]\n138:     \n139:     subgraph Parallel_Strands[\"Vice City Syndicate Alliances (3 Parallel Strands)\"]\n140:         direction TB\n141:         subgraph Strand_Tyrone[\"Strand 1: Tyrone (Muscle)\"]\n142:             M51[\"51. Tyrone\"] --> M52[\"52. Here, Kitty Kitty\"]\n143:         end\n144:         \n145:         subgraph Strand_Boobie[\"Strand 2: Boobie & Dre'Quan (Syndicate)\"]\n146:             M54[\"54. Top Billing\"] --> M55[\"55. Boobie Time\"]\n147:             M55 --> M56[\"56. First Impressions\"]\n148:         end\n149:         \n150:         subgraph Strand_Raul[\"Strand 3: Raul & Randy (Cartel & Cars)\"]\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
